; NS_UNREACHABLE — one live nameserver, one that is gone.
;
; test.zone delegates this to ns1 and to ns-dead, and 127.0.0.9 has nothing
; listening. dns-auth serves the zone properly, so the domain resolves fine
; today: that is the whole hazard. A dead nameserver in a delegation is
; invisible until the last live one goes too.
;
; The zone has to exist here. Without it dns-auth refuses the name as well, and
; the fixture would be testing a lame delegation rather than a dead server.
$ORIGIN stale.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns1.test. hostmaster.propgate.invalid. (
                1 7200 3600 1209600 300 )
@       IN NS   ns1.test.
@       IN NS   ns-dead.test.

www     IN A    198.51.100.72
